RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8116349Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8126975Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8234785Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8245396Z ^[[0m
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8245976Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8247103Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8247458Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8247766Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8248562Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8249046Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8249642Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8250305Z    if you are ready to continue.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8250610Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8251218Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8252123Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8252708Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8253094Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8253386Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8253620Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8253894Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8254123Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8254571Z    can use Nix.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8254738Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8254866Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8255043Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8260933Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8262882Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8263333Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8263505Z I will:
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8263794Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8264094Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8264577Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8265219Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8265690Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8266017Z  - install Nix in /nix
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8266331Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8266765Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8267223Z    /root
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8276522Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8277513Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8288531Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8289489Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8289777Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8290766Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8291324Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8309861Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8310752Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8321758Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8322564Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8323017Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8323265Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8323531Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8323909Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:18:08.8324229Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
